# Decisions

## {{DATE}} — Use the workspace as the durable source of truth

**Decision:** Keep stable project context in versionable workspace files. Treat chat history and agent-specific memory as non-authoritative caches.

**Reason:** The project must remain understandable when switching agents, interfaces, or sessions.

## {{DATE}} — Keep one canonical agent instruction file

**Decision:** Use the workspace-root `AGENTS.md` as the only canonical agent-instruction source.

**Reason:** Tool-specific copies drift. Hosts that cannot discover `AGENTS.md` should use a thin external adapter or project setting.

## {{DATE}} — Adopt the `{{PROFILE}}` workspace profile

**Decision:** {{PROFILE_DECISION}}

**Reason:** Start with the smallest durable structure that matches the current work without guessing a technology stack or creating redundant folders.

## {{DATE}} — Record work as tasks in docs/tasks

**Decision:** Track each work task as a file under `docs/tasks/` and list it in `docs/tasks/INDEX.md`. Do not treat a chat session as the task boundary. The same task may span multiple sessions.

**Reason:** Work needs to be resumable across agents and sessions without relying on chat memory or a user reminder to start a task list.
